What is a Printed Circuit Board?
Printed Circuit Boards serve as the fundamental building blocks of modern electronic equipment. They consist of copper clad laminates, insulating substrate materials, and a series of etched conductors that create complex signal and power routing networks. Depending on the application, PCBs can be rigid, flexible, or a hybrid (rigid flex), and they may incorporate advanced features such as micro vias, high density interconnects (HDI), and embedded components to meet the demanding performance requirements of AI data centers, electric vehicle powertrains, and high frequency telecommunications.
